# Attendance module (P6) — demo requests (VS / Rider / VS Code REST Client).
#
# One-time local setup (Development) is the same as users.http (connection string + seeded admin in user secrets).
# Run:  dotnet run --project src/Hosts/Host.CairoUniversity          (migrations apply on startup in Development)
#
# Prerequisites: scheduling.http + lifecycle.http (a slot for today's weekday in the active term, a professor who
# teaches its group, and students registered in that group). Paste the ids/tokens below.
# A QR token lives 20 seconds: fetch a fresh one right before each check-in.

@host = http://localhost:5080
@adminToken = paste-the-admin-token-here
@professorToken = paste-the-teaching-professors-token-here
@studentToken = paste-a-registered-students-token-here
@studentId = paste-that-students-id-here
@slotId = paste-a-slot-id-here
@groupId = paste-that-slots-group-id-here
@sessionId = paste-the-session-id-from-the-open-call-here
@qrToken = paste-the-token-from-the-qr-call-here
@deviceChangeId = paste-a-device-change-id-here

### Professor: open today's session for the slot → 201 (date defaults to today; any occurrence of the slot is allowed)
POST {{host}}/api/attendance/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slotId": "{{slotId}}" }

### Professor: the rotating QR → 200 { token, expiresAt } (closed session → 409)
GET {{host}}/api/attendance/sessions/{{sessionId}}/qr
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}

### Student: check in with the QR → 200 { status: present | late } (expired 400, outsider 403, other phone 403, twice 409)
POST {{host}}/api/attendance/check-in
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "{{qrToken}}", "deviceFingerprint": "android-demo-7f3a9c21" }

### Professor: audited manual entry (present/late → manual_audit, absent → absent); the note is required
POST {{host}}/api/attendance/sessions/{{sessionId}}/manual
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "studentId": "{{studentId}}", "status": "present", "note": "هاتفه تعطل — حاضر في القاعة" }

### Professor: live roster → everyone with present / late / manual_audit / absent / not_yet + counts
GET {{host}}/api/attendance/sessions/{{sessionId}}/live
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}

### Professor: close → absents filled in, summary; closing again returns the same summary
POST {{host}}/api/attendance/sessions/{{sessionId}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}

### Student: own history + percentage per subject (closed sessions only)
GET {{host}}/api/attendance/history
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### Professor (own group) or admin: percentage per student
GET {{host}}/api/attendance/groups/{{groupId}}/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}

### Professor (own groups) or admin (all): students below the faculty's effective threshold
GET {{host}}/api/attendance/at-risk?groupId={{groupId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}

### Student: ask to move attendance to a new phone → 201 pending (one pending at a time, one approved per term)
POST {{host}}/api/attendance/device-change
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newFingerprint": "iphone-demo-0b44e1aa", "reason": "My phone was stolen" }

### Admin: the request queue
GET {{host}}/api/admin/attendance/device-changes?status=pending
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Admin: approve (old phone revoked, new one registered) — or POST …/reject
POST {{host}}/api/admin/attendance/device-changes/{{deviceChangeId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Teacher / admin: the group's attendance sheet as CSV (one status column per closed session) — P10.4
GET {{host}}/api/attendance/groups/{{groupId}}/export
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}

### Teacher (own groups) / admin: finals eligibility; barred = below the faculty's threshold — P10.5
GET {{host}}/api/attendance/eligibility?groupId={{groupId}}&barredOnly=true
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}
